        "subject": "LU-20852 mdt: report a stale FLR file on its last close",
        "message": "LU-20852 mdt: report a stale FLR file on its last close\n\nA file with a stale FLR mirror or EC parity stays stale until some\nexternal tool runs \"lfs mirror resync\" on it.  The client that last\nwrote the file is a good place to resync it at once, while the data\nis likely still in its cache, but it has no way to know that the file\nneeds it.\n\nOn the last close of a file opened for write, have mdt_mfd_close()\ncheck whether the layout is still WRITE_PENDING or SYNC_PENDING, and\nif so set OBD_MD_CLOSE_NEED_RESYNC in the CLOSE reply.  This reuses\nthe OBD_MD_FLXATTRRM bit, which is only sent in setxattr requests, so\nold clients ignore it and no connect flag is needed.  The bit is only\na hint: it is not set if a reader closes the file last, and it is\nlost if the reply is resent, so files still need a periodic scan.\nIf the client caches the open handle, the CLOSE is sent only when the\nhandle is dropped, so a file that is repeatedly opened, written and\nclosed is not reported (and resynced) after every close.\n\nLOD already tracks the FLR state of a cached layout, so have\nlod_attr_get() return it as la_flr_state, which mdd_close() fetches\nanyway.  Read the layout xattr only when LOD has not cached it.  Reset\nldo_flr_state when a plain or foreign layout is loaded, so a layout\nswapped in from a plain file does not keep a stale state.\n\nThe client counts these closes in the llite.*.stats\n\"close_need_resync\" counter.  A later patch will use this notification\nto optionally resync the mirror or parity.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-flr\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ib7be29020b1e4da379e444e5fb575482083ebbe5\n"
      },
